    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Apartment 128, Block B3, Belgrove Park is a bright and well-presented two-bedroom, two-bathroom apartment extending to approximately 73.9 sq m / 795 sq ft, with the added benefit of a west-facing balcony. Situated within the popular Belgrove Park development beside St. Anne’s Park, the property enjoys a highly convenient Clontarf location with excellent natural light throughout.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation is well laid out, beginning with a welcoming entrance hall leading into a spacious open-plan living and dining area. This main reception space is bright and comfortable, with timber flooring and extensive glazing enhancing the sense of light and space. The dining area opens directly onto the west-facing balcony, providing a valuable outdoor extension to the living space. The balcony is not included in the stated internal floor area.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen is positioned just off the living area and is fitted with a range of timber-fronted wall and floor units, worktops and a selection of integrated and freestanding appliances. It offers good storage and a practical layout while remaining closely connected to the main living space.\r\n\r\nThere are two well-proportioned double bedrooms located off the inner hallway, both benefiting from natural light and built-in storage. The main bedroom includes an en suite shower room, while the second bathroom is located off the hallway and is fitted with a bath, wash-hand basin and WC. Both bathrooms are presented in a clean, functional style.\r\n\r\nThe property is in good condition throughout and offers a balanced layout of living, sleeping and outdoor space. A key advantage is the inclusion of two parking spaces, a rare and valuable feature in the area. The annual service charge is approximately €2,300.\r\n\r\nThe location is a major highlight, with St. Anne’s Park immediately nearby offering extensive green space, walking routes and sports facilities. The Clontarf seafront, Dollymount Strand and Bull Island are also within easy reach, along with a wide range of local shops, cafés and restaurants. Regular bus services provide convenient access to Dublin city centre and surrounding areas.\r\n\r\nApartment 128 represents a well-located and practical home in a highly regarded residential setting."
      },
      {
